1. Problem Statement
You are given a rod of length n inches and an integer array price[] of size n. The value price[i - 1] represents the selling price of a piece of length i.
You may cut the rod into smaller pieces and sell those pieces. Determine the maximum total value that can be obtained by cutting and selling the entire rod.
Note: The length of the rod is equal to the number of elements in price[]. Each piece length may be used any number of times.
2. Input and Output
Input: An integer array price[] of size n.
Output: A single integer representing the maximum obtainable value.
3. Sample Test Cases
Sample 1
Input:
price[] = [1, 5, 8, 9, 10, 17, 17, 20]

Output:
22
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

 
public class Main
{
    public static int value(int price[], int n){
        
        if(n == 0){
            return 0;
        }
        
        int maxval = 0;
        
        for(int i=1; i<n; i++){
            
            int profit = price[i-1] + value(price, n-1);
            maxval = Math.max(maxval, profit);
        }
        
        return maxval;
    }
    
	public static void main(String[] args) {
		 
		 
	 int price[] = {6,8,4,3};
	 int n = price.length;
	 
		 
	}
}
